              "blocks": {
                "text_CW8WcV": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "Text",
                  "settings": {
                    "visibility": "always-display",
                    "text": "<p>Peculiar People started in 2023 while I was serving a mission in San Antonio, Texas. The name comes from Peter's description of the Saints as \"a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people\" — members who keep their covenants without making a show of it, and are fine looking a little old-fashioned for it.</p><p>We make apparel with original line art of Latter-day Saint temples, made one temple at a time and printed on heavier, better-made garments. Most members want to talk about the gospel but don't know how to open the door. A shirt someone asks about is an easier start than a knock on one.</p><p>— Evan<br/><br/><a href=\"/pages/our-story\" title=\"Our Story\">Read more about our story here →</a></p>",
